We finally have the real answer, straight from the package maintainer. The key setting inside the block is **`ldap_filter`** — not `passdb_ldap_filter`, not plain `filter`, not `args`. We genuinely never tried this exact spelling before. And there's also `ldap_bind = no`, which is the direct 2.4 equivalent of our old `auth_bind = no`.

## Corrected config, built from the real template

```
cat > /etc/dovecot/conf.d/auth-ldap.conf.ext << 'EOF'
ldap_uris = ldap://smtp-mtq-1.ool.fr
ldap_auth_dn = cn=dovecot-auth,ou=services,o=ool
ldap_auth_dn_password = dovecote
ldap_base = ou=acc,o=ool

passdb ldap {
  ldap_filter = (&(mail=%{user})(|(accountStatus=active)(accountStatus=enabled))(!(deliveryMode=forwardonly)))
  ldap_bind = no

  fields {
    user = %{ldap:mail}
    password = %{ldap:userPassword}
  }
}

userdb ldap {
  ldap_filter = (&(mail=%{user})(|(accountStatus=active)(accountStatus=enabled))(!(deliveryMode=forwardonly)))

  fields {
    home = %{ldap:mailMessageStore}
  }
}
EOF
```

Then:

```
doveconf -n
```

Run both and show me the result — fingers crossed this is finally the one.

