Confirmed — exactly the mismatch we suspected. Let's add a per-user override inside our LDAP userdb block specifically, so the other (passwd-file) domains stay untouched.

## Fix

```
cat > /etc/dovecot/conf.d/auth-ldap.conf.ext << 'EOF'
ldap_uris = ldap://localhost
ldap_auth_dn = cn=dovecot-auth,ou=services,o=ool
ldap_auth_dn_password = dovecote
ldap_base = ou=acc,o=ool

passdb ldap {
  ldap_filter = (&(mail=%{user})(|(accountStatus=active)(accountStatus=enabled))(!(deliveryMode=forwardonly)))
  ldap_bind = no
  fields {
    user = %{ldap:mail}
    password = %{ldap:userPassword}
  }
}

userdb ldap {
  ldap_filter = (&(mail=%{user})(|(accountStatus=active)(accountStatus=enabled))(!(deliveryMode=forwardonly)))
  fields {
    home = %{ldap:mailMessageStore}
    mail_path = %{ldap:mailMessageStore}/Maildir
  }
}
EOF
```

## Validate and reload

```
doveconf -n | grep -A 8 "^userdb ldap"
systemctl reload dovecot
```

Run both and show me the result.

Confirmed — no global fallback at all for `mail_uid`/`mail_gid`. Without an explicit mapping, Dovecot would likely fail or behave unpredictably trying to access mail files for `ool.fr` accounts. Let's fix it, matching the same `vmail:vmail` convention already used by `only.fr`.

## Fix

```
cat > /etc/dovecot/conf.d/auth-ldap.conf.ext << 'EOF'
ldap_uris = ldap://localhost
ldap_auth_dn = cn=dovecot-auth,ou=services,o=ool
ldap_auth_dn_password = dovecote
ldap_base = ou=acc,o=ool

passdb ldap {
  ldap_filter = (&(mail=%{user})(|(accountStatus=active)(accountStatus=enabled))(!(deliveryMode=forwardonly)))
  ldap_bind = no
  fields {
    user = %{ldap:mail}
    password = %{ldap:userPassword}
  }
}

userdb ldap {
  ldap_filter = (&(mail=%{user})(|(accountStatus=active)(accountStatus=enabled))(!(deliveryMode=forwardonly)))
  fields {
    home = %{ldap:mailMessageStore}
    mail_path = %{ldap:mailMessageStore}/Maildir
    uid = vmail
    gid = vmail
  }
}
EOF
```

## Validate and reload

```
doveconf -n | grep -A 10 "^userdb ldap"
systemctl reload dovecot
```

Run both and show me the result.

